smb: client: fix DFS interlink failover

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10
commit-author Paulo Alcantara <pc@manguebit.com>
commit 4f42a8b54b5c6e36519aef3cb1f6210e54abd451
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.115.1.el8_10/4f42a8b5.failed

The DFS interlinks point to different DFS namespaces so make sure to
use the correct DFS root server to chase any DFS links under it by
storing the SMB session in dfs_ref_walk structure and then using it on
every referral walk.

	Signed-off-by: Paulo Alcantara (Red Hat) <pc@manguebit.com>
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit 4f42a8b54b5c6e36519aef3cb1f6210e54abd451)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

